# The floor every SisyphusMD project's .gitignore must contain, checked by
# packaging/check-gitignore-base.py. Project-specific artifacts go in the project's own
# .gitignore below its base block — this file is only the shared minimum.
#
# Ignore files are NOT a security control. Secrets are kept out by allowlisted build contexts and
# by not writing them into the tree in the first place. These patterns are the last net, not the
# first, and they exist because the cost of one slip is unbounded.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/

# Environments
.venv*/
venv/

# Tool caches and coverage
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Key and certificate material. *.p12 and *.p8 matter for any project that signs or notarises a
# macOS artifact: an Apple signing certificate and an App Store Connect key are exactly the two
# files a release engineer ends up with locally, and neither belongs in a repository.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.p8

# Locally built distributables
*.deb
*.rpm
*.pkg
*.tar
*.tar.gz

# Release and smoke outputs the shared release machinery writes at the repository root: buildx
# --output destinations (out/ for CI, out-<arch>/ for a release leg, package-smoke-<fmt>-<arch>/,
# homebrew-smoke-result/) and the release notes publish.yml renders before uploading them. Each is
# recreated from scratch on every run, so a copy in the tree is always stale.
/out/
/out-*/
/package-smoke-*/
/homebrew-smoke-result/
/notes.md
